# The build context is the repo root, because the image needs `agent/` (which carries the
# capability and transport trees) and `vocabulary/`. These are the parts it never needs, and
# sending them is pure cost on a Pi.
#
# NOTE: onboarding/ is deliberately NOT ignored here. Excluding it from the context would hide
# the boundary in a file nobody reads; it is excluded by the Containerfile not naming it, where
# a test can see the decision. See tests/test_layout.py.

.git
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.egg-info

# Firmware CODE is flashed to a board, not built into an image — but since #175 each firmware
# directory may carry an ontology.ttl, a third T-Box source the loader merges, and an agent
# whose world types a board by its firmware class derives NOTHING without it (the sensing
# world's fern subscribed to nothing, silently, which is how this exception was found).
# Everything else stays out, and one exclusion is load-bearing for secrets: a generated
# include/config.h carries the wifi and a device credential, and must never reach a layer.
# One level deep, not `firmware/**`: excluding the per-firmware DIRECTORIES prunes them from
# the walk entirely, so a `!` exception under them can never fire — measured, not read in a
# manual. This shape leaves the directories traversable and excludes their contents, and the
# negation wins on the one file it names.
firmware/*/*
firmware/*.md
!firmware/*/ontology.ttl
**/.pio

# an agent's belief base is created at birth, never baked in
**/state

# secrets are MOUNTED per world, never copied into a layer
world/*/secrets
keys

# not needed at runtime
# A package may carry its own tests as plain files beside its code, so this is per-FILE rather
# than a directory: `COPY packages/` would otherwise put pytest cases in the agent image.
**/test_*.py
knowledge
infra/grafana
infra/mosquitto
